{"kind":"report","text":"approved at exact head 98dbf6004369cef1028f5e13dbd762a579d6c764 (request/gs-wait, three commits over main e2e00899), under hugh's request 16942b09 as amended by hugh's assert 8a64ee37. Repair round after verdict 6d11d23e.\n\nProvenance: filed under codex's key by a Claude session on hugh's explicit instruction of 2026-09-17. The review was done by the same fresh-context reviewer as 6d11d23e, which did not implement the head.\n\nGate at the head: go build ./... and go vet clean; go test ./cmd/gs/ ./cmd/gitseq-mcp/ ./internal/service/ ./internal/statusview/ -timeout 40m -count=1 exit 0 (cmd/gs 451.8s, gitseq-mcp 53.2s, service 45.5s, statusview 0.6s, no reruns); go test -race on the service head/wait/actionable tests and the cmd/gs wait tests clean. Tree clean; 11 paths changed since f15d21e9, all inside the 18-artifact set.\n\nArchitecture: same layers (resident /v0/actor-wait poll, statusview filter, MCP adapter, CLI). The repair changes the poll contract in one place: under actionable, a declined poll advances its own baseline (server.go:523-525) and the timeout delta is built from the caller's original cursor (server.go:414). The head-clock cost invariant is restored and measured: a 5 s actionable poll behind a declined live change costs 21 ref reads, the same as a quiet any poll; three actionable waiters cost 23. architecture.md and wait.md Cost state this accurately.\n\nSecurity: trust boundaries unchanged. The cursor file now carries the session's public presence handle (wait.go:81), which the room already publishes; the credential is never written. classifyResident (wait.go:325) separates cancellation from resident failure, so an interrupt departs and does not fall back locally. Renewal refusals reopen rather than exit. Own-session exclusion under any matches presence changes by handle only; frames carry conversation ids, so a real frame cannot be mis-excluded. MCP sends any as an absent field, so an explicit until=any works against an older resident.\n\nSimplification: ActionableWait, the per-head cache, frontierMoved's reset clause and most restating comments are gone; one FilterWait serves four callers. Residue, P3 only: Server.filter builds a full BuildWait per judged tick only to read PriorityChat.Frames when pending is already in hand (server.go:538-544); Server.filtered exists for one test (server.go:118); the MCP degraded path keeps its own filteredHead cache (main.go:2271).\n\nFindings 1-9 of 6d11d23e: all fixed or resolved, each with a red proof. 1 ref-read per tick: mutant no-baseline-advance -\u003e TestActionablePollBehindALiveChangeDoesNotReadOnEveryTick, ...JudgesADeclinedChangeOnce. 2 any self-wake: probe three quiet calls each exit 3 after 1.5 s; mutant -\u003e TestWaitUnderAnyIsNotWokenByItsOwnSessions. 3 renewal fatal: probe now times out; mutant -\u003e TestWaitReopensASessionRefusedAtRenewal. 4 own-act wake: mutant -\u003e TestAcceptedWaitEventsIgnoresTheActorsOwnActs, TestWaitIsNotWokenByTheActorsOwnAct. 5 MCP unpinned: M8 -\u003e TestDegradedWaitHonoursTheUntilFilter, M9 -\u003e TestWaitToolAdvertisesTheUntilFilter, any-as-word -\u003e TestWaitToolSendsAnyAsAnAbsentField. 6: cache removed; M5 -\u003e TestAcceptedWaitEventsIgnoresWhatRestsOnARetiredEventOfYours and the CLI twin. 7: resolved by amendment 8a64ee37; renderWake (wait.go:556-585) matches the amended text. 8: fixed (any as absent field). 9: mutant -\u003e TestWaitDepartsItsSessionWhenInterrupted. No test was removed or loosened; f15d21e9's 20 tests remain.\n\nNew findings, none blocking:\n1. P3 internal/statusview/actor.go:719: the waiting-on clause of actionableRowEvents has no red proof (dropping it survives the suite). Category: a report from your performer on a request you filed. The head behaves correctly (scratch test proved it); add the test.\n2. P3 docs/reference/gs/wait.md:82,110-114 still says any wakes on any live change including a reset and frames the client-side decision as old-resident-only; code never wakes any on resets or this command's own sessions (wait.go:421-424). Two sentences.\n3. P3 server.go:525: under actionable a timeout answer's live list omits declined live changes; MCP callers lose presence deltas between cursor and timeout. Harmless for gs wait; undocumented in mcp/wait.md.\n4. P3 wait.go:212-214: a reopen failing on transport exits 1 where f15d21e9 fell back locally; narrow window.\n5. P3 simplification residue as above.\n\nMergeable as is. The P3s can follow on a later request. Probe sources and mutant script: /tmp/codex-gs-wait-98dbf600.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:279a466b2a0b610a54279089f25762d0862e66fe","binding":"assigned","head":"98dbf6004369cef1028f5e13dbd762a579d6c764","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:57900e30e94e00ef7043d9a357ae5d99be11f8fa\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0385e206ef76ef7cdd0367a66ab535997cd3dfc9\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:57900e30e94e00ef7043d9a357ae5d99be11f8fa","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}